      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Defenders argue that this critique misrepresents the doctrine, as originalism is a commitment to a specific *method* of inquiry, not to a particular policy outcome. They assert that by adhering to the original public meaning, judges are constrained to the text and are forced to argue within the boundaries set by the historical consensus, rather than imposing personal preference. In this view, the \"partisan outcomes\" are the predictable results of the political will that was dominant at the time of the Constitution's ratification.",
