      "content": "i get that, but isn't it kind of problematic though? like, we live in a totally different world now than the 1700s. if judges only look at what people thought hundreds of years ago, doesn't that basically just freeze our rights in time and prevent the law from evolving with modern society? it feels like a much more flexible approach would be more legitimate for a modern democracy.",
